                <td style="padding:4px 16px 4px 0;color:#64748b;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;">Your members join as</td>
                <td style="padding:4px 0;color:#0f172a;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;font-weight:600;">editor</td>
              </tr>
            </table>
            <p style="margin:0 0 16px;padding:0 0 0 16px;border-left:3px solid #e2e8f0;color:#334155;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;">Would love your crew on the punch-card pipeline.</p>
            <p style="margin:0 0 16px;color:#334155;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;">Accepting lets you choose which of your teams to bring and which of its members join. Nobody on your team gets access until you do.</p>
            <p style="margin:0 0 16px;color:#334155;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;">You are being asked to make this the project’s primary team, which means its billing identity fills in contracts and its pay periods drive invoicing.</p>
            <p style="margin:0 0 16px;color:#334155;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;">If you do not have an account yet, sign up with this email address and your invitation will be waiting for you.</p>
            <div style="margin:28px 0 0;">
